    "answer": {
      "short": "$a>-20$.\n\nComplete the square to obtain $r^2=a+20$, which must be positive.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4x+y^2-8y&=a\\\\(x-2)^2-4+(y-4)^2-16&=a\\\\(x-2)^2+(y-4)^2&=a+20\\end{align*}$$\nThe centre is $(2,4)$ and $r^2=a+20$. A nondegenerate circle requires $r^2>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a+20&>0\\\\a&>-20\\end{align*}$$\nAt $a=-20$, the relation represents only the point $(2,4)$, a degenerate circle, so this boundary is excluded.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
